            <div xml:id="d404">

                <pb facs="0501" n="399" sameAs="frus:frus1927v03/pg399"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/4879: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Eberhardt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-05-31T16:00:00-05:45"><hi rendition="#italic">May 31, 1927—4
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 8:25 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>142. In accordance with agreement made before General Stimson the Liberal <hi
                        rendition="#italic">jefes politicos</hi> for 6 departments recommended by
                    Moncada are being named by President Diaz tomorrow. Moncada had endeavored to
                    name chief of police and collectors of internal revenue in each department also
                    but, as these were specifically omitted in all conferences and only <hi
                        rendition="#italic">jefes politicos</hi> schedule specifically agreed upon
                    with Diaz, I have insisted that only <hi rendition="#italic">jefes
                        politicos</hi> be named and Moncada has agreed though he will probably cable
                    Stimson regarding the subject.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Eberhardt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
